# Keep development files and repository metadata out of the public Worker.
#
# Without this the deploy fails with "Asset too large":
#   - .git/objects/pack/*.pack is ~141 MiB, over the 25 MiB per-file limit;
#   - scripts/download/*.jsonl are ~1.4 GiB and ~1.0 GiB (raw Wiktionary
#     dumps used to regenerate the dictionary, never served).
#
# See wrangler.toml and CLOUDFLARE.md.
.git/
.dev/
.claude/
.github/
.agents/
.codex/
.vscode/
.wrangler/
node_modules/
graphify-out*/
test-results/
scripts/
doc/

# Screenshots kept at the repo root for the docs. This is deliberately NOT a
# blanket "*.png": img/*.png are the dictionary pictograms the app loads at
# runtime, and a global *.png excluded all 1,743 of them, so every one
# answered 404 in production. The largest is 70 KB, far below Cloudflare's
# 25 MB per-file limit, so there is no reason to exclude the folder.
shot-*.png

*.md